G4820.definition:
συν-βάλλω 
 (Rec. συμ-), [in LXX:  2Ch.25:19  (גָּרָה hith.),  Isa.46:6  (זוּל),  Jer.43:3  (סוּת hi.),  Wis.5:8 , al. ;] 
 to throw together, hence,  
 __(a) of speech (before λόγους, Eur., al.),  to discuss, confer  (sc. λόγους): with dative of person(s),  Luk.11:53 , WH, mg.,  Act.17:18;  before πρὸς ἀλλήλους,  Act.4:15;  
 __(b)  to reflect, consider, ponder : ἐν τ. καρδίᾳ,  Luk.2:19;  
 __(with)  to meet with, fall in with :  Act.20:14;  in hostile sense, εἰς πόλεμον, with dative (εἰς μάχην, Polyb.),  Luk.14:31;  
 __(d) mid.,  to contribute  (Polyb., al.; cf. MM, xxiv):  Act.18:27. †
 (AS)

G4864.definition:
συν-αγωγή , -ῆς, ἡ 
 [in LXX chiefly for עֵדָה, also for קָהָל, etc. ;] 
prop., a bringing together; 
 __1. of things, 
 __(a)  a gathering in of harvest ; 
 __(b) a collection of money. 
 __2.  Of persons,  
 __(a)  a collecting, assembling  (Polyb.); 
 __(b)  an assembly  (MM, xxiv; Deiss.,  LAE , 101 ff.):  Rev.2:9 3:9 ; esp. of a Jewish religious assembly,  a synagogue :  Luk.12:11 ,  Act.9:2 , al.; of a Christian assembly,  Jas.2:2.  By meton., of the building in which the assembly is held,  a synagogue :  Mat.10:17 ,  Mrk.1:21 , al. (cf. Cremer, see word ἐκκλησία) 
   SYN. : ἐκκλησία (which see)   (AS)
